# Code owners for security-critical files. GitHub requires the listed
# accounts to review and approve any PR that touches these paths. Branch
# protection on `main` should be configured to require code-owner
# review for these files specifically.
#
# Rationale: the round-8 audit observed that golden artifacts
# (`private_multisig.idl.json`), the verifier source
# (`methods/guest/src/bin/private_multisig.rs`), Cargo.lock, and
# `deny.toml` are now load-bearing for the on-chain ABI contract and the
# supply-chain trust chain. A solo-approver PR that mutates any of
# these in a coordinated way (e.g., handler + IDL together) could
# regress security invariants while CI stays green. CODEOWNERS forces a
# second human into the review loop for those paths.

# The golden IDL is the audited on-chain ABI shape. Changing it without
# a corresponding (reviewed) verifier handler change indicates drift.
/private_multisig.idl.json                               @nizarsyahmi37

# The verifier program — every handler signature is part of the ABI.
# `methods/guest/` carries both the verifier source AND the SPEL rev
# pin + nssa_core tag pin in its Cargo.toml. `methods/Cargo.toml` pins
# `risc0-build = "=3.0.5"` — drift here changes the image-id.
/methods/                                                @nizarsyahmi37

# Host-side program crate and its api_stability sentinels (which now
# enforce the IDL shape, SPEL/nssa SHAs, risc0 four-site pin, and
# nullifier-entry PDA seed shape — see THREAT_MODEL §11).
/private_multisig_program/                               @nizarsyahmi37

# Core types: the ABI error codes (E1xxx-E4xxx) referenced in
# THREAT_MODEL and consumed by the SDK + on-chain verifier.
/private_multisig_core/                                  @nizarsyahmi37

# SDK: hosts `APPROVE_CIRCUIT_IMAGE_ID_PINNED` (the host-side image-id
# pin enforced by `sdk/tests/image_id_pin_parity.rs`) and pins
# `risc0-zkvm = "=3.0.5"` in its Cargo.toml.
/sdk/                                                    @nizarsyahmi37

# IDL generator and CLI: both carry the SPEL rev pin in their
# Cargo.toml deps. A rev bump in any of these without a coordinated
# Cargo.lock update bypasses the lockfile SHA sentinel.
/idl-gen/                                                @nizarsyahmi37
/cli/                                                    @nizarsyahmi37

# Workspace root: member list + resolver setting. Removing a member
# silently excludes it from `cargo test --workspace`.
/Cargo.toml                                              @nizarsyahmi37

# Resolved dep graph — captures the audited SHAs for git deps that
# cannot be source-pinned in manifests (notably nssa_core).
/Cargo.lock                                              @nizarsyahmi37

# Supply-chain policy.
/deny.toml                                               @nizarsyahmi37

# Workflow + dependabot config — the CI is the only continuous
# guardrail; tampering with the workflow would silence other checks.
/.github/                                                @nizarsyahmi37
